\begin_layout Standard
Pico 2 W contains an on-board 2.4GHz wireless interface using the Infineon CYW43439,
 which has the following features:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
WiFi 4 (802.11n),
 Single-band (2.4 GHz)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
WPA3
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
SoftAP (Up to 4 clients)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bluetooth 5.2
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Support for Bluetooth LE Central and Peripheral roles
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Support for Bluetooth Classic
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The antenna is an onboard antenna licensed from ABRACON (formerly ProAnt).
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The wireless interface is connected via SPI to the RP2350.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Due to pin limitations some of the wireless interface pins are shared.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The CLK is shared with VSYS monitor so only when there isn’t an SPI transaction in progress can VSYS be read via the ADC.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Infineon CYW43439 DIN/DOUT and IRQ all share one pin on the RP2350.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Only when an SPI transaction isn’t in progress is it suitable to check for IRQs.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The interface typically runs at 33MHz.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
There are three GPIO pins from the CYW43439 that are used for other board functions and can easily be accessed via the SDK:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
WL_GPIO2
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
IP VBUS sense - high if VBUS is present else low
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
WL_GPIO1
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
OP controls the on-board SMPS power save pin (Section 3.4)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
WL_GPIO0
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
OP connected to user LED
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Power-Up Sequence and Timing
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Sequencing of Reset and Regulator Control Signals
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The CYW43439 has two signals that allow the host to control power consumption by enabling or disabling the Bluetooth®,
 WLAN and internal regulator blocks.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
These signals are described below.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Notes:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The WL_REG_ON and BT_REG_ON signals are OR’ed in the CYW43439.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The diagrams show both signals going high at the same time (as would be the case if both REG signals were controlled by a single host GPIO).
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

If two independent host GPIOs are used (one for WL_REG_ON and one for BT_REG_ON) only one of the two signals needs to be high to enable the CYW43439 regulators.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The CYW43439 has an internal power-on reset (POR) circuit.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

The device will be held in reset for a maximum of 110 ms after VDDC and VDDIO have both passed the POR threshold .
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

Wait at least 150 ms after VDDC and VDDIO are available before initiating SDIO accesses.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
VBAT and VDDIO should not rise faster than 40 µs.
 VBAT should be up before or at the same time as VDDIO.
 VDDIO should not be present first or be held high before VBAT is high.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Description of Control Signals
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
WL_REG_ON:
 Used by the PMU to power up the WLAN section.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 It is also OR-gated with the BT_REG_ON input to control the internal CYW43439 regulators.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 When this pin is high,
 the regulators are enabled and the WLAN section is out of reset.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

When this pin is low the WLAN section is in reset.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

If both the BT_REG_ON and WL_REG_ON pins are low the regulators are disabled.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
BT_REG_ON:
 Used by the PMU (OR-gated with WL_REG_ON) to power up the internal CYW43439 regulators.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

If both the BT_REG_ON and WL_REG_ON pins are low the regulators are disabled.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 When this pin is low and WL_REG_ON is high the Bluetooth® section is in reset.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Note:
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For both the WL_REG_ON and BT_REG_ON pins there should be at least a 10 ms time delay between consecutive toggles (where both signals have been driven low) to allow time for the CBUCK regulator to discharge.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If this delay is not followed there may be a VDDIO in-rush current on the order of 36 mA during the next PMU cold start.
\end_layout

