\begin_layout Subsection
WLAN Initialization and Reset
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Once power is stable,
 take the Wi-Fi core out of its reset state:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Assert WL_REG_ON:
 Drive the WL_REG_ON pin high.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Asserting WL_REG_ON powers up the internal regulators dedicated to the WLAN section and releases the Wi-Fi core from reset.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
(Note:
 De-asserting this pin will hold the WLAN section in reset;
 it features an internal 200 kΩ pull-down resistor by default.)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
 Configure the SDIO Communication Interface
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Unlike Bluetooth (which uses UART),
 the Wi-Fi core requires a high-speed Secure Digital Input Output (SDIO) interface.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Configure the Host Controller to communicate via the following pins:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
SDIO Clock (SDIO_CLK).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
SDIO Command (SDIO_CMD).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
SDIO Data Lines (SDIO_DATA).
\end_layout

